## Architecture Patterns

### Project Structure

```
src/
├── api/              # HTTP handlers/controllers
│   └── v1/           # API version namespace
├── domain/           # Business logic & entities
│   ├── entities/     # Domain objects
│   └── services/     # Domain services
├── infrastructure/   # External concerns
│   ├── database/     # DB connections & repositories
│   ├── cache/        # Caching layer
│   └── external/     # Third-party integrations
├── middleware/       # Request/response middleware
├── utils/            # Shared utilities
└── types/            # TypeScript type definitions
```

### Design Principles

1. **Separation of Concerns** - API handlers should not contain business logic
2. **Dependency Injection** - Services receive dependencies through constructor
3. **Repository Pattern** - All data access goes through repositories
4. **Single Responsibility** - Each module/class has one reason to change

### Allowed Patterns

- Factory functions for object creation
- Strategy pattern for interchangeable algorithms
- Observer pattern for event handling
- Repository pattern for data access

### Prohibited Patterns

- God objects (classes doing too much)
- Circular dependencies between modules
- Direct database access from API handlers
- Hardcoded configuration values

