## Security Standards

### OWASP Compliance

| Category | Requirement | Implementation |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| A01:Broken Access Control | Check permissions on every request | Auth middleware |
| A02:Cryptographic Failures | Use strong encryption | bcrypt, AES-256 |
| A03:Injection | Parameterized queries only | ORM/prepared statements |
| A07:Auth Failures | Rate limiting, secure tokens | express-rate-limit, JWT |

### Authentication

- JWT tokens with RS256 signing
- Access tokens expire in 15 minutes
- Refresh tokens expire in 7 days
- Tokens stored in httpOnly cookies (not localStorage)

### Password Requirements

- Minimum 12 characters
- At least one uppercase, one lowercase, one number
- Hashed with bcrypt (cost factor 12)
- No password in logs or error messages

### Input Validation

```typescript
// All user input must be validated at API boundary
const schema = z.object({
  email: z.string().email(),
  password: z.string().min(12),
  name: z.string().min(1).max(100),
});
```

